        <briefdescription>
<para>Create a new mTLS connection to the specified endpoint. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Performs the full connection lifecycle:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>TCP connect to endpoint</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>TLS handshake with mutual authentication</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Verify peer certificate</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>endpoint</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target endpoint (e.g., &quot;localhost:50051&quot;)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Fully established <ref refid="mtls__connection__factory_8h_1a71f21e09bf365489dab9d85bd4785e24" kindref="member">SSL</ref> connection, or nullopt on failure:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>nullopt: Connection failed, timeout, or handshake error</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>unique_ptr&lt;SSL&gt;: Valid connection ready for use</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Caller owns the returned connection and must release it back to the pool via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_endpoint_connection_pool_1aee0faf8f2a8c4cacd5fb09ab08ed86d3" kindref="member">EndpointConnectionPool::releaseConnection()</ref></para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Implementation should not throw; return nullopt on errors </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
